# Direct dependencies of converter/app.py. Edit this file, then run
# ./lock-requirements.sh to regenerate the pinned closure in requirements.txt.
# Docker installs requirements.txt, never this file.
#
# Ranges here express what the code actually needs. The pins in
# requirements.txt express what we ship. Keeping them apart is what lets a
# dependency bump be reviewed as a diff of resolved versions rather than as an
# invisible change of meaning inside a `>=`.

# DXF read/repair and the SVG rendering backend.
#
# Deliberately NOT ezdxf[draw]. That extra exists for the matplotlib and Qt
# backends, and app.py uses neither — it imports
# ezdxf.addons.drawing.svg.SVGBackend, which is pure Python. The extra pulled
# in PyMuPDF (AGPL-3.0, forbidden outright by §2.1) and PySide6
# (LGPL-3.0/GPL-2.0/GPL-3.0, never approved), both of which were being built
# into the shipped converter image for code that is never imported.
ezdxf>=1.3.0,<2

# IFC parsing and geometry iteration (§6.7.4 — IFC is a first-class format).
# LGPL-3.0-or-later: used unmodified, loaded dynamically, which is the only
# form §2.1 permits. Recorded in docs/licences.md.
ifcopenshell>=0.8.0,<0.9

# Array maths behind the geometry paths.
